    "result": "Perfect! All frai-core tests are now passing. Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Fixed Issues\n\n1. **Missing named exports in `src/finetune/index.js`**: The test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available in the default export. Added explicit re-exports of the constants (`APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, `RISK_LEVELS`) from the schema module.\n\n2. **Incorrect toxicityMetric parameter handling in `src/eval/metrics.js`**: The `toxicityMetric` function was being called with both outputs and references by `runEvaluations`, but it interprets the second parameter as custom banned terms. This caused the references array to be treated as banned terms, producing incorrect results. Fixed by wrapping `toxicityMetric` in `DEFAULT_METRICS` to only pass outputs, while allowing the exported function to still accept custom banned terms.\n\n**Test results**: All 28 tests across 8 test files now pass \u2713",
